\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Odd periods and the unobserved corners}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In an odd direction the samples on opposite sides of #{\pi} have opposite sines. Their linear interpolant vanishes at the midpoint, with negative local orientation (\ref{fdip-0142}). Both endpoint cosines equal #{-\cos(\pi /N_j)}, so the interpolated Wilson mass contributed there is #{1+\cos(\pi /N_j)} in dimensionless units. That zero is absent from the vertex sum. For periods #{1} or #{2}, every sampled sine on that axis is zero; the local simplicial degree used in \ref{fdip-019Y} assumes #{N_j\ge3}.}

\p{For even periods the partial binomial sum in \ref{fdip-019Y} also occurs in an odd-dimensional domain-wall calculation. The mass windows and the meaning of the current in that comparison are described in \ref{fdip-01AA}.}
